@brief
A ticket, not an exercise.

    REF-77  Someone pasted RefundProvider into the repo from Slack.
            Make it fit the codebase and finish it, then fix the doc
            that goes with it.

Two files, opened in that order. `:wn` writes the current one and
moves to the next.

  1. refund.provider.ts — the indentation is gone or wrong on every
     line of the class. The header comment is one long line and must
     wrap at 72 columns, `//` on every line. And `expire` is missing
     its `values` line, which belongs directly after `where: { id },`:

         values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED' },

     Both long names already appear in the file. Do not type them out.

  2. REFUNDS.md — three misspelled words. Spell checking is on. Take
     the first suggestion for each.

Par assumes you reflow with an operator, re-indent with an operator,
complete the long names, and fix the typos without typing them.

@keys
| `gqip` | reflow the header paragraph |
| `gg=G` | re-indent the whole file |
| `Ctrl-N` | complete a long name from the buffer |
| `]s` `1z=` | next typo, first suggestion |
| `:wn` | write, then move to the next file |

@hints
Reflow the header first, from line 1: it is a paragraph on its own.
Then re-indent the entire file in one command, before adding the new
line, so the line you add inherits a correct indent from `autoindent`.
--
`/async expire` then `/where` puts you on the line the new one goes
under. `o` opens below it at the right depth. Type `cancellationR`
and let `Ctrl-N` finish it; the word is in the header comment, and
completion does not care that it is in a comment. Same for
`REFUND_W`.
--
`:wn` to the doc. `]s1z=` three times. `:wq`.

@solution
    gqip gg=G
    /async expire<Enter> /where<Enter>
    ovalues: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationR<Ctrl-N>: 'REFUND_W<Ctrl-N>' },<Esc>
    :wn<Enter>
    ]s1z= ]s1z= ]s1z= :wq<Enter>

About 115 keystrokes, roughly forty of which are the new line.

Nothing here is a new key; the chapter gave you all of it. What the
ticket tests is whether you reach for the operator instead of the
hand-fix: `gq` instead of `J` and Enter twenty times, `=` instead of
`>>` on thirty lines, `Ctrl-N` instead of retyping a twenty-letter
identifier you can see on the screen, `1z=` instead of retyping a word
you have just proved you cannot spell.

Order matters once. `gg=G` before `o`, because the new line takes its
indent from the line above it, and that line has to be right first.
Everything else could have been done in any sequence.

One thing to notice about the completion: `cancellationReason` was
only in a comment, and `REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED` only in the same
comment. Keyword completion reads words, not code, which cuts both
ways — it will also happily offer you a typo from three lines up.

@start refund.provider.ts
// Refund window. Orders can be refunded for thirty days after they are placed. Past that point cancelling still works, but no money moves and the order records cancellationReason REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED so finance can reconcile it at month end.

import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
constructor(
@inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
@inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
) {}

public async findOne(id: string) {
const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

if (!order) {
throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
}

return order;
}

public isInsideWindow(placedAt: Date) {
return Date.now() - placedAt.getTime() <= 30 * 86_400_000;
}

    public async refund(id: string) {
            const order = await this.findOne(id);

        if (!this.isInsideWindow(order.placedAt)) {
    return this.expire(id);
            }

        await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

            return this.orderRepository.update({
    where: { id },
        values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
        }

  public async expire(id: string) {
      return this.orderRepository.update({
    where: { id },
      });
    }
}

@expected refund.provider.ts
// Refund window. Orders can be refunded for thirty days after they are
// placed. Past that point cancelling still works, but no money moves
// and the order records cancellationReason REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED so
// finance can reconcile it at month end.

import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from '../order/order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class RefundProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public isInsideWindow(placedAt: Date) {
    return Date.now() - placedAt.getTime() <= 30 * 86_400_000;
  }

  public async refund(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (!this.isInsideWindow(order.placedAt)) {
      return this.expire(id);
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async expire(id: string) {
    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED', cancellationReason: 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED' },
    });
  }
}

@start REFUNDS.md
# Refunds and the thirty day window

A refund request is proccessed by the payment provider, not by us. We
store the reciept id on the order when the provider calls back, and
the order moves to CANCELLED immediatly whether or not money moves.

Outside the window nothing is charged back. The order still moves to
CANCELLED and the reason is recorded for finance.

@expected REFUNDS.md
# Refunds and the thirty day window

A refund request is processed by the payment provider, not by us. We
store the receipt id on the order when the provider calls back, and
the order moves to CANCELLED immediately whether or not money moves.

Outside the window nothing is charged back. The order still moves to
CANCELLED and the reason is recorded for finance.
